# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AI Usage Panel — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env` for local dev (npm run dev), and/or paste the same
# key/value pairs into Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables.
# Never commit a real `.env`.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── 1. Panel login (REQUIRED) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The single password that protects the panel. Generate both values with:
#     npm run hash-password -- "your-chosen-password"
# AUTH_PASSWORD_HASH is `scrypt$<salt_hex>$<hash_hex>` (never the plaintext).
AUTH_PASSWORD_HASH=
# Random 32-byte hex secret used to sign session tokens:
#     openssl rand -hex 32
AUTH_TOKEN_SECRET=

# ── 2. Database (REQUIRED) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Neon Postgres POOLED connection string (host must contain `-pooler`).
# Neon dashboard → your project → Connection Details → Connection string.
# Keep `?sslmode=require` at the end.
DATABASE_URL=

# ── 3. AIHubMix (REQUIRED) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Console (console.aihubmix.com) → Settings → "Generate System Access Token".
# Format: fd*** — this is the MANAGE KEY, not your model API key (sk-***).
AIHUBMIX_MANAGE_KEY=
# Optional override; defaults to https://aihubmix.com
AIHUBMIX_BASE_URL=

# ── 4. DeepSeek (REQUIRED) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# platform.deepseek.com → API keys. Used for the balance/quota endpoint.
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# OPTIONAL — enables per-model + per-day DeepSeek spend (uses DeepSeek's internal
# console usage API, which needs a browser session token, not the API key).
# See README → "DeepSeek per-model usage". Leave blank to hide that section.
DEEPSEEK_PLATFORM_TOKEN=

# ── 5. Optional hardening ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Protects /api/collect so only the Vercel cron can trigger it.
# Set a random value here AND the same value as CRON_SECRET in Vercel.
CRON_SECRET=
# Comma-separated list of browser origins allowed to call the API, only needed
# if the page is hosted on a DIFFERENT origin than the API. Leave blank when the
# page and /api are served by the same Vercel project (the default).
ALLOWED_ORIGIN=
